<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12043" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cursŭālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		cursus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to a course,
				running</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				<i>post-horses</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 12, 51, 19</span></i>
			: raeda, <i>a stage-coach</i>, Cod. Th. 12, 12,
			9: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollicitudo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>speed in running</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 6, 29, 7</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Hasty, speedy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ministerium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 5, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
